// # oodar/docs — Per-Package Documentation
//
// Logline: Per-package documentation for the oodar v2.1.0+ substrate. Five .oot files (SECURITY_MODEL, PILLARS, CAPABILITIES_TABLE, BUILD_AND_INSTALL, TESTING) cover the 8D Red Team documentation surface, the cap+Landlock security model, the polyrepo build convention, and the 25-token cap inventory.
//
// Setup: Per RFC-0005, per-package docs replace global LLMS.oot-style codex dumps. The 5 .oot files are the v2.1.0+ authoritative references; each file is <= 256 lines per RFC-0003.
//
// Beats:
//   1. SECURITY_MODEL.oot      — the 25-token cap system, the 4 hard rules, the 6-step cap flow.
//   2. PILLARS.oot             — how oodar maps to the 10 NORTHSTAR Pillars (5-of-10 wired: 3, 4, 5, 7, 9).
//   3. CAPABILITIES_TABLE.oot  — the 25 cap tokens, 5 reserved bits, grant/require/attenuate/used-by table.
//   4. BUILD_AND_INSTALL.oot   — canonical `gcc oodar.c`, per-file compile, polyrepo, liboodar.a.
//   5. TESTING.oot             — the 8D Red Team matrix and the 5 tier-5 tests_challenger_*.c files.
//
// ──▓▓ oodar/docs ANCHOR ──▓▓──
// :: 5 .oot files, 981 total lines, all <= 256 ::
